on cfix(integration): align backend with the frontend, notifications, dashboard, green builds

The frontend and backend had diverged: the frontend called routes the backend
never exposed, and used slightly different names. The rule applied throughout is
that the backend aligns with the frontend - no screen of Dylane's was rewritten.

Contract audit: 64 backend routes, 48 frontend calls checked, 0 missing.

Routes that did not exist (created)
  GET /workspace                  - operations screen, every role
  POST /corrections/attachments   - evidence upload (PDF/image, 5 MB)
  PATCH /corrections/shifts/:id   - attendance correction
  GET /corrections/shifts/:id     - correction history

Naming mismatches (backend aliases added, frontend untouched)
  /auth/me, /auth/activate-account, /auth/invitations/:id/resend,
  /user/:id/status, /users/:id/activate, /users/imports/template,
  /stations/:id/status

Two blocking bugs
  1. GET /auth/me was missing. session.tsx calls it on every tab visibility
     change and treats a failure as a dead session (.catch(() => clear())), so
     users were silently logged out whenever they returned to the tab.
  2. Creating a user from the UI was impossible. UserCreateModal posts
     accountStatus, RegisterDto did not declare it, and main.ts runs
     ValidationPipe with forbidNonWhitelisted, so every creation returned 400.
     The field is now accepted and authoritative (ACTIVE | PENDING).

Notifications (etape E)
  Notification model + migration, and GET /notifications,
  GET /notifications/unread-count, PATCH /notifications/:id/read,
  PATCH /notifications/read-all - all scoped to req.user.id.
  Wired into the real events via the existing choke points:
    - openReplacementRequest() notifies supervision, covering both origins
      (declared impediment and automatic absence) exactly once.
    - assignReplacement() notifies the incoming swapper, releases the outgoing
      one and confirms to supervision.
  Notifications are emitted after the transaction commits, so a rollback never
  announces a change that did not happen. notify() swallows its own errors: a
  notification is a side effect and must not fail the business action.

Dashboard (etape F)
  GET /dashboard/stats: shifts of the day split into expected/present/late/
  absent/completed, open and resolved replacement requests, weekly hours
  against the station limit, workforce headcounts and a dated timeline.
  Scoping reuses resolveAccessibleStationIds; a SWAPPER sees only their own
  shifts. "Today" is computed in Douala local time, not raw UTC.
  New DashboardPage at <space>/tableau-de-bord for every role.

Frontend build repaired (it did not compile before this work)
  - Template-literal backticks had been stripped in commit 7286c29 (52 in HEAD
    against 20 in the working tree). Planner.tsx restored from HEAD.
  - Modal.tsx in the working tree had lost its footer slot and backticks;
    HEAD was correct, restored from HEAD.
  - day-roster.css was referenced by Planner.tsx but absent from the repo
    (deleted after 9fc77cc). Recovered from git history as UTF-8.
  - api/auth-api.ts method widened to POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE,
    MockCtx.method aligned, Modal size widened to sm|md|lg|xl with the missing
    .modal-panel--sm rule, Planner imported as a default export,
    exportToExcel called with its real object signature.
  Result: tsc --noEmit 0 errors, npm run build exit 0, no CSS warnings.

Business rules audit (etape G)
  All 11 rules verified against the live API, including: 7h and 9h refused,
  overlap and second-shift-same-day refused, 6h rest refused on a station with
  minRestHours=8, a swapper already at 48h/48h refused, approved leave blocks a
  shift, END without START flips the row to ABSENT, the scheduler marks past
  EXPECTED rows ABSENT, a declared impediment writes no attendance row, and
  ShiftChange keeps type/previous/new/author.

Improvements found while testing
  - AD_HOC source: covering a shift by hand now records a ReplacementRequest
    instead of leaving no trace in the queue.
  - The seed violated its own weekly limit (7 x 8h = 56h on a 48h station); it
    now respects it.
  - /shifts/mine applied a different filter than /workspace, so swappers saw
    shifts they could not declare an impediment on (400). Both now agree.

Adds scripts/audit-contract.cjs and scripts/audit-business-rules.cjs so these
checks can be replayed, plus docs/FRONTEND-BACKEND-RECONCILIATION.md. Updates
docs/REPLACEMENT-WORKFLOW.md, whose "not covered" section was stale.